<h2>The real cost of Mailchimp plus extras</h2>

<p>Mailchimp's pricing looks attractive in isolation. The Standard plan starts at $20 USD per month for 500 contacts. But that only covers email. Once you add the tools you actually need to run a small business, the total climbs fast.</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Mailchimp Standard:</strong> $20/month</li>
  <li><strong>Calendly (booking):</strong> $12/month</li>
  <li><strong>Separate CRM:</strong> $30-80/month</li>
  <li><strong>Funnel builder:</strong> $49-97/month</li>
  <li><strong>Review management:</strong> $40-80/month</li>
</ul>

<p>That is $151 to $289 per month for five separate tools. Plus the time cost of managing five logins, five sets of data, and zero native integration between them.</p>

<p>DUSA replaces all of those with a single platform at a lower combined cost. More importantly, it eliminates the gaps between tools where leads get lost and follow-ups get missed.</p>

<h2>When Mailchimp is the right choice</h2>

<p>Mailchimp is the right choice if email marketing is your only need. If you run a content-driven business, send a weekly newsletter, and do not need CRM, booking, funnels, or SMS, Mailchimp does that job well. Its free tier is a sensible starting point for businesses that are just beginning to build an email list and are not ready to invest in a full platform yet.</p>

<h2>When DUSA is the right choice</h2>

<p>DUSA is the right choice if you need more than email. If you are a service-based business, a local operator, or a sole trader who needs to manage leads, book appointments, follow up automatically, request reviews, and run your pipeline from one place, DUSA does all of that without requiring you to stitch together a stack of separate tools.</p>

<blockquote><p>If you are already paying for three or more tools alongside Mailchimp, that is a sign you have outgrown email-only and are ready for a platform.</p></blockquote>

